1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,879
Engineers fire chickens at airplanes at 350 miles per hour.

2
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:08,779
Why do they do it? birds hit planes about 60 times a day, in the u.s. alone.

3
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:13,019
In 2009, geese shut down both engines of a jet over New york.

4
00:00:13,343 --> 00:00:16,460
The first windshields broke at just 75 miles per hour.

5
00:00:16,879 --> 00:00:20,160
Now every cockpit window must stop a 4-pound bird.

6
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:23,820
So they test it with a real chicken, fired from a giant air cannon.

7
00:00:24,339 --> 00:00:27,960
One rule: the chicken can't be frozen. real birds aren't ice.

8
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:30,160
That's why, before you fly,
